WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.570
NARRATOR: Choose a point at x equals a and a
second point h units away.

2
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.586
NARRATOR: The line through them is a secant
line.

3
00:00:08.586 --> 00:00:12.894
NARRATOR: Its slope divides the change in
function value by the change in input.

4
00:00:12.894 --> 00:00:18.444
NARRATOR: That number describes average change
across the interval, not yet what happens at

5
00:00:18.444 --> 00:00:19.633
one exact point.

6
00:00:19.754 --> 00:00:23.345
NARRATOR: Now shrink h without setting it
equal to zero.

7
00:00:23.345 --> 00:00:29.083
NARRATOR: As the second point approaches the
first, the secant lines approach a limiting

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:30.723
position: the tangent line.

9
00:00:30.723 --> 00:00:36.668
NARRATOR: If their slopes approach one finite
value, that value is the derivative f prime of

10
00:00:36.668 --> 00:00:37.040
a.

11
00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:41.918
NARRATOR: The limit turns nearby average
change into instantaneous change.

12
00:00:42.026 --> 00:00:47.082
NARRATOR: A positive derivative means the
function is increasing locally; a negative

13
00:00:47.082 --> 00:00:52.560
derivative means it is decreasing; and a zero
derivative gives a horizontal tangent.

14
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:56.731
NARRATOR: Close to the point, the tangent line
can approximate the curve.

15
00:00:56.731 --> 00:01:01.816
NARRATOR: The derivative is therefore both a
geometric slope and a practical rate of

16
00:01:01.816 --> 00:01:02.179
change.
